# The other half of the linear-accumulator pass: a Fold From: a channel,
# writing cells into a dense Grid one setat at a time. The accumulator here is
# the current pipeline value, so the fold clones it once on entry — a sibling
# Part or Channel could be holding the same grid — and then writes through.
#
# A digit grid rather than a character one, so both sides carry the same cell
# layout and the number measures the writes instead of a string header.
Cursed Energy: stdin
Cursed Technique: Split Text by "\n"
Cursed Technique: Split Each by ""
Channeled Energy: Convert To Integers
Channeled Energy: Convert To Grid

Channel "marks":
    Cursed Technique: Apply
        Using: (g) -> range(0, rows(g) * cols(g))

Maximum Technique: Fold
    From: marks
    Using: (g, i) -> setat(g, (i * 7) % rows(g), (i * 13) % cols(g), 0 - 1)
Maximum Technique: Count Cells
    Using: (c) -> c < 0
Reveal: stdout
